<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abd al-Aziz ibn Mutib Al Rashid</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1870">1870</a>–<a href="/years/1906">1906</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abd <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-aziz">al-Aziz</a> ibn Mutib <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashidi-dynasty">Al Rashid</a> was emir of Jabal Shammar, ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hail">Ha'il</a>, from 1897 to 1906. He inherited the dominant power in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabia">Arabia</a> from his uncle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-ibn-rashid">Muhammad ibn Rashid</a> but lost <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/riyadh">Riyadh</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-saud">Ibn Saud</a> in 1902. Despite Ottoman support, he was killed in battle against Ibn Saud at Rawdat Muhanna in 1906.</p></div>
